# Copy this to export/.env and fill in the password. That file is gitignored.
#
# The simulator reads its OWN .env rather than reaching into the ingestion
# repo's config. Depending on another project's file would couple two repos
# through a filesystem path and would not survive this running anywhere else.
#
# Connect as mtg_consumer, NOT as the pipeline role.
#
# This is a guard, not a formality. mtg_consumer has USAGE on mtg_v1 and no
# grant whatsoever on mtg_internal, so an exporter query that reaches for a
# physical table fails immediately with "permission denied for schema
# mtg_internal" instead of working until a migration reshapes a column
# underneath it. Running as mtg_pipeline would make that failure impossible to
# detect locally and inevitable in deployment.
#
# The password is URL-encoded, so a value with reserved characters survives.
# Precedence: an explicit --database-url, then $MTGSIM_DATABASE_URL in the real
# environment, then this file. A stale file never overrides an explicit one.
MTGSIM_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://mtg_consumer:PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5433/mtg
